&lt;h1&gt;


  My Hacktoberfest 2026 Journey: Getting Started with Open Source
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Hey everyone!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I'm a Computer Science undergraduate at IIIT Lucknow, and I've been spending time learning programming, solving DSA problems, and building projects.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Now, I want to take the next step by contributing to open source.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Hacktoberfest feels like a good opportunity to explore real-world projects, understand how developers collaborate, and learn how software is built beyond personal projects and tutorials.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What I Want to Learn
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here are a few things I want to focus on during this journey:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exploring open-source repositories and understanding their codebases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Finding issues where I can make meaningful contributions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving my Git and GitHub workflow, especially branches and pull requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning how to read existing code and debug unfamiliar projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connecting with developers and learning from their experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Technologies I'm Interested In
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My current interests include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;C++ and Data Structures &amp;amp; Algorithms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React and Next.js&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Web Development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Web3 and Blockchain Development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-powered applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I'm happy to explore projects outside these areas if they offer an opportunity to learn something new.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Looking for Recommendations
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Since I'm getting more involved in open source, I'd appreciate recommendations for repositories that welcome new contributors.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I'd love to hear about your experiences and learn from the community.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My goal is to make genuine contributions, improve my development skills, and become more comfortable working on collaborative projects.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Looking forward to seeing what I can learn along the way.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


  hacktoberfest #opensource #beginners
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I recently built &lt;strong&gt;MoneyMov&lt;/strong&gt;, a free personal finance tracker to help people understand where their money is going.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The idea was simple:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Know where your money moves.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of building another complicated finance application, I wanted to create something simple enough for everyday use.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What Is MoneyMov?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;MoneyMov is a personal finance tracker where users can manage their:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💰 Income&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💸 Expenses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📊 Spending categories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📈 Investments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🤝 Committees / Bachat&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💵 Lending / Loans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The additional modules are optional, so users can use only the parts they actually need.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, someone may only want to track expenses, while another person may also want to keep track of investments or money they've lent to someone.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Tech Stack
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I built the application using the MERN stack:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;MongoDB&lt;/strong&gt; — Database&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Express.js&lt;/strong&gt; — Backend API&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;React.js&lt;/strong&gt; — Frontend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Node.js&lt;/strong&gt; — Backend runtime&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Axios&lt;/strong&gt; — API requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Tailwind CSS&lt;/strong&gt; — UI styling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Recharts&lt;/strong&gt; — Charts and data visualization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;JWT&lt;/strong&gt; — Authentication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;bcrypt&lt;/strong&gt; — Password hashing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The frontend is deployed on &lt;strong&gt;Netlify&lt;/strong&gt;, while the backend is deployed on &lt;strong&gt;Render&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Authentication &amp;amp; Security
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One of the things I focused on while building the project was authentication and basic application security.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Some of the things implemented include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Password hashing with bcrypt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;HTTP-only authentication cookies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JWT-based authentication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protected API routes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Environment variables for secrets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forgot-password functionality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hashed password-reset tokens&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Token expiration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Helmet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rate limiting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MongoDB input sanitization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;HTTP Parameter Pollution protection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;User-specific data access&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, the backend doesn't simply trust the user ID coming from the frontend.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The authentication middleware verifies the token and gets the authenticated user's ID before accessing their data.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Spending Visualization
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One of the dashboard features is a category-based spending breakdown.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Shopping      Rs 400
Food          Rs 1,200
Transport     Rs 500
Bills         Rs 2,000
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The data is also visualized using a pie chart so users can quickly understand where most of their spending went.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Some Challenges
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Building the application wasn't completely straightforward.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I ran into several issues during development and deployment, including:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MongoDB Atlas connection timeouts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Render deployment and networking issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SMTP connection problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Authentication cookies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CORS configuration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Express proxy configuration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SPA routing on Netlify&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mobile authentication behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handling protected routes correctly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These problems were actually a useful part of the project because they forced me to understand what was happening beyond simply writing React components.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, deploying a MERN application locally is very different from deploying the frontend and backend separately.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You have to think about how each layer communicates in production:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Frontend
   ↓
API requests
   ↓
Backend
   ↓
Authentication
   ↓
Database
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Each layer introduces its own configuration, security considerations, and potential issues.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why I Built It
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I wanted to build something that was more than just another CRUD project.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;While working on MoneyMov, I got to work with:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Authentication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;REST APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MongoDB&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Email verification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Password reset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data visualization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsive UI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production debugging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It also gave me a chance to work through problems that don't usually appear when everything is running on localhost.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What's Next?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There are still several things I want to improve.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Some ideas include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Better dashboard analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;More useful financial reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improved mobile experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Better transaction filtering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;More visualizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exporting financial data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional security improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;MoneyMov is currently free, and my goal is to keep the core personal finance features simple and accessible.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Final Thoughts
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This project started as an idea for a simple expense tracker, but it gradually became a much bigger learning experience.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The biggest thing I learned is that building a real application isn't only about making the UI work.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You also have to think about:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Authentication → Security → APIs → Database → Deployment → Users&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That's where a lot of the interesting engineering problems begin.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you're also building a MERN application, I'd be interested to hear what problems you've run into while deploying your project.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Try MoneyMov
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;MoneyMov is free to use. Give it a try and let me know what you think!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;🔗 &lt;strong&gt;Website:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://moneymov.netlify.app" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://moneymov.netlify.app&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MoneyMov — Know where your money moves.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When building vertical web applications, separating feature comparisons into standalone, fast-loading micro-sites is an effective way to keep your core application bundle lean while addressing specific user intents.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Recently, while building out supporting comparison pages for an educational test simulator, I designed a reusable data schema in TypeScript to render head-to-head feature matrices and inject structured JSON-LD data automatically.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is the architectural pattern and data model used to build these static comparison micro-sites.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  1. Defining the Comparison Data Model in TypeScript
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of hardcoding HTML tables for each competitor analysis, defining a strict TypeScript interface ensures every micro-site renders consistent evaluation metrics (pricing model, learning format, regulatory updates, and pass guarantees):&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;interface&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ComparisonMetric&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;featureName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;primaryPlatformValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;competitorValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;highlightAdvantage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;interface&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ComparisonSiteConfig&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;slug&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;competitorCategory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;legacy-portal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;career-directory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;trade-school&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;lastUpdatedYear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;metrics&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ComparisonMetric&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[];&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;By typing the &lt;code&gt;competitorCategory&lt;/code&gt;, the UI components can dynamically adjust the layout depending on whether we are comparing two software tools or comparing digital self-study against an offline curriculum.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  2. Live Production Deployments (Built on Lovable)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Using this modular structure, I deployed three separate micro-sites targeting different segments of the HVAC certification space:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Demo 1 (Legacy Portal Comparison):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://hvacexammaster-vs-epatest.lovable.app/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;HVAC Exam Master vs EPATest.com — EPA 608 Prep Compared (2026)&lt;/a&gt; — Compares interactive active-recall testing (Core, Type I, II, and III modules) against static Web 1.0 study guides.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Demo 2 (Lead-Gen Directory Comparison):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://hvacexammaster-vs-hvaccareernow.lovable.app/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;HVAC Exam Master vs HVAC Career Now (2026 Comparison)&lt;/a&gt; — Contrasts direct certification utility tools against school lead-generation portals.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Demo 3 (Offline Institution Comparison):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://hvacexammaster-vs-hvactechnicalinstitute.lovable.app/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;HVAC Exam Master vs HVAC Technical Institute — 2026 Comparison&lt;/a&gt; — Evaluates self-paced digital exam prep ROI against traditional brick-and-mortar tuition costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  3. Automating FAQ &amp;amp; Comparison JSON-LD Schema
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To help search engines and AI answer engines parse the comparison matrices accurately, each micro-site injects a structured &lt;code&gt;FAQPage&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;WebPage&lt;/code&gt; JSON-LD payload into the document head:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;TypeScript&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ComparisonSchema&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;schemaData&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@context&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;https://schema.org&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;WebPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;specialty&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;EPA Section 608 Certification Prep&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;script&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"application/ld+json"&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;dangerouslySetInnerHTML&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;__html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;schemaData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


  Key Takeaways for Frontend Builders
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Decouple Content from Layout:&lt;/strong&gt; A shared TypeScript schema lets you spin up multiple comparison landing pages in minutes.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Keep Micro-Sites Focused:&lt;/strong&gt; Rather than building one massive table comparing ten different business models, isolating each comparison into its own deployment keeps page speed high and user intent clear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⚡ &lt;strong&gt;TL;DR:&lt;/strong&gt; Your laptop lies about speed. Measure what real users feel with LCP, INP, and CLS, then spend effort on the few highest-leverage fixes that actually move those numbers instead of micro-optimizing things users never notice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Contents
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The site that lied to you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The principle: measure what users feel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The page-load timeline, mapped to the user&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The three vitals at a glance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Two fixes that pay for themselves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Common mistakes that cost hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Takeaways&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Where to go next&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The site that lied to you
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You build a page. On your laptop it is instant, text snaps in, images pop, buttons respond the moment you click. You ship it. Then a user opens it on a three-year-old Android phone over patchy mobile data, and it is a different product entirely: a blank screen for two seconds, then a hero image that shoves the headline down just as they reach for it, then a tap that does nothing for half a second because the main thread is busy parsing your JavaScript.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Nothing changed about your code between those two experiences. What changed was the &lt;strong&gt;device&lt;/strong&gt; and the &lt;strong&gt;network&lt;/strong&gt;. Your laptop has a fast CPU, a fast connection, and a warm cache. Most of your users have none of those. The gap between "works on my machine" and "works for my users" is exactly the gap &lt;strong&gt;Core Web Vitals&lt;/strong&gt; were invented to close.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📌 &lt;strong&gt;Who this is for:&lt;/strong&gt; Junior frontend engineers who can build a working page but have never deliberately measured its speed. If you have ever shipped something that felt fast to you and slow to everyone else, this is the article that explains why, and what to do about it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The principle: measure what users feel
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Measure what users actually feel, on the devices they actually use, not what your laptop tells you on a good day.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The one rule of performance work&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Performance is not a single number like "page weight" or "load time". It is a sequence of moments the user lives through: &lt;em&gt;Can I see it yet? Is it stable while I read? Does it respond when I touch it?&lt;/em&gt; Core Web Vitals are three metrics, each one standing in for one of those felt moments. They are deliberately user-centric, they do not care how clever your build is, only what the human in front of the screen experiences.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;In the real world&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;In tech&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;How fast the main dish actually arrives at your table&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;LCP, when the largest, most meaningful content appears&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The waiter responding quickly when you ask for the bill&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;INP, how fast the page reacts to your interactions&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Your table not wobbling and spilling your drink mid-meal&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;CLS, the layout staying put instead of jumping around&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Loading a page is like being seated at a restaurant.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A restaurant where the food is fast, the staff are responsive, and the table is steady feels good even if you cannot name why. Get any one of the three wrong and the whole experience sours, exactly how a page with great LCP but a janky layout still feels broken.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The page-load timeline, mapped to the user
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is one page load as the user lives it, left to right in time. Each vital attaches to a different moment of that journey, load, stability, and interactivity are not the same event and you cannot fix them with the same lever.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fmermaid.ink%2Fimg%--UGFnZSByZXNwb25kcyB0byB0aGUgdGFwIikKICBjbGFzcyBuX2lucCBjb21wdXRlOwogIG5faGFwcHkoIlBhZ2UgZmVlbHMgZG9uZTxici8-RmFzdCDCtyBzdGFibGUgwrcgcmVzcG9uc2l2ZSIpCiAgY2xhc3Mgbl9oYXBweSBvYnNlcnZhYmlsaXR5OwogIG5fcmVxdWVzdCAtLT4gbl9ibGFuawogIG5fYmxhbmsgLS0-IG5fbGNwCiAgbl9sY3AgLS4tPnwic2hpZnRzIGh1cnQgaGVyZSJ8IG5fY2xzCiAgbl9sY3AgLS0-IG5faW50ZXJhY3QKICBuX2ludGVyYWN0IC0tPnwicmVzcG9uc2UgZGVsYXkifCBuX2lucAogIG5faW5wIC0tPiBuX2hhcHB5%3FbgColor%3D0d1017%26type%3Dpng" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fmermaid.ink%2Fimg%--UGFnZSByZXNwb25kcyB0byB0aGUgdGFwIikKICBjbGFzcyBuX2lucCBjb21wdXRlOwogIG5faGFwcHkoIlBhZ2UgZmVlbHMgZG9uZTxici8-RmFzdCDCtyBzdGFibGUgwrcgcmVzcG9uc2l2ZSIpCiAgY2xhc3Mgbl9oYXBweSBvYnNlcnZhYmlsaXR5OwogIG5fcmVxdWVzdCAtLT4gbl9ibGFuawogIG5fYmxhbmsgLS0-IG5fbGNwCiAgbl9sY3AgLS4tPnwic2hpZnRzIGh1cnQgaGVyZSJ8IG5fY2xzCiAgbl9sY3AgLS0-IG5faW50ZXJhY3QKICBuX2ludGVyYWN0IC0tPnwicmVzcG9uc2UgZGVsYXkifCBuX2lucAogIG5faW5wIC0tPiBuX2hhcHB5%3FbgColor%3D0d1017%26type%3Dpng" alt="A single page load over time: each Core Web Vital maps to a distinct moment the user perceives." width="1626" height="230"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;A single page load over time: each Core Web Vital maps to a distinct moment the user perceives.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Notice the order. LCP happens early (loading), CLS accumulates across the whole load (stability), and INP is measured every time the user interacts (responsiveness). You optimize them in roughly that sequence, but you only know which one to attack after you measure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Measure&lt;/strong&gt;: Run Lighthouse in Chrome DevTools, but more importantly pull &lt;strong&gt;field data&lt;/strong&gt; from the &lt;a href="https://pagespeed.web.dev" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;PageSpeed Insights&lt;/a&gt; report or the CrUX dashboard. Field data is real users on real devices, that is the truth. Lab data is a controlled simulation; useful for debugging, dangerous as your only source.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Find the biggest offender&lt;/strong&gt;: Look at which of the three vitals is in the "poor" or "needs improvement" band. Do not optimize a green metric. In the Lighthouse report, expand the failing metric to see what element or script is responsible, it names the exact LCP element and the longest tasks blocking the main thread.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Fix one thing&lt;/strong&gt;: Apply the highest-leverage change for that specific vital, an oversized hero image, a render-blocking bundle, an unsized embed. Change one variable so you can attribute the result.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Re-measure&lt;/strong&gt;: Re-run the same measurement and confirm the number actually moved. Then repeat from step two on the next-worst metric. Performance work is a loop, not a one-time pass, and field data updates over 28 days, so real-world wins take time to show.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The three vitals at a glance
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Each vital has published thresholds. Google grades the &lt;strong&gt;75th percentile&lt;/strong&gt; of your users, meaning three out of four real visits must hit the "good" bar before the metric counts as passing. Optimizing for the average hides your slowest users; the 75th percentile is what forces you to care about that mid-range phone.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Metric&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What it measures&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Good threshold&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Top fixes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;LCP (Largest Contentful Paint)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Loading, how long until the largest visible element (usually a hero image or headline block) is painted&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;≤ 2.5 s&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Optimize/compress the LCP image, preload it, use a CDN, remove render-blocking CSS/JS, serve modern formats (WebP/AVIF)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;INP (Interaction to Next Paint)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Interactivity, how quickly the page visually responds to taps, clicks, and key presses across the whole visit&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;≤ 200 ms&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Break up long tasks, reduce main-thread JS, code-split, defer non-critical scripts, debounce expensive handlers&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Visual stability, how much content unexpectedly jumps around as the page loads&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;≤ 0.1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Set width/height on images &amp;amp; video, reserve space for ads/embeds, avoid injecting content above existing content, preload fonts&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The three Core Web Vitals, their thresholds, and where to spend your effort.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The bands are the same shape for all three: &lt;strong&gt;good&lt;/strong&gt; is the threshold above, &lt;strong&gt;needs improvement&lt;/strong&gt; is the grey middle, and &lt;strong&gt;poor&lt;/strong&gt; is anything past the second cutoff (LCP &amp;gt; 4 s, INP &amp;gt; 500 ms, CLS &amp;gt; 0.25). INP replaced the older FID metric in 2024, FID only measured the &lt;em&gt;first&lt;/em&gt; interaction's delay, while INP watches every interaction, which is a far harsher and more honest test.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Two fixes that pay for themselves
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The two highest-leverage techniques for a junior to reach for are &lt;strong&gt;lazy-loading offscreen images&lt;/strong&gt; (helps LCP and total bytes) and &lt;strong&gt;code-splitting heavy components&lt;/strong&gt; (helps INP by shrinking the JavaScript the main thread must parse upfront). Both are one-liners in modern stacks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Lazy-load images you cannot see yet
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An image below the fold does not need to load before the user scrolls to it. The native &lt;code&gt;loading="lazy"&lt;/code&gt; attribute defers it for free. The critical detail: &lt;strong&gt;always set &lt;code&gt;width&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;height&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; so the browser reserves the space, this is what prevents the layout shift (CLS) when the image finally arrives. One important exception: your LCP image (the hero) should &lt;em&gt;not&lt;/em&gt; be lazy, load it eagerly, even preload it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;below-the-fold.html&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight html"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;&amp;lt;!-- Hero image: the LCP element. Load it eagerly + hint high priority. --&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;img&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;src=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"/hero.avif"&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;width=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"1200"&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;height=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"600"&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;fetchpriority=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"high"&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;alt=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"Product dashboard"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c"&gt;&amp;lt;!-- Offscreen images: defer until the user scrolls near them. --&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c"&gt;&amp;lt;!-- width + height reserve the box so nothing jumps (protects CLS). --&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;img&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;src=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"/screenshot.avif"&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;width=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"800"&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;height=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"450"&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;loading=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"lazy"&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;alt=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"Feature screenshot"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  Code-split so the main thread can breathe
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A 500 KB JavaScript bundle has to be downloaded, parsed, and executed before the page is interactive, and parsing JS is one of the most expensive things a phone's CPU does. If a heavy component (a chart library, a rich editor, a modal) is not needed on first paint, load it on demand with a &lt;strong&gt;dynamic import&lt;/strong&gt;. The bundler splits it into a separate chunk that only ships when it is actually used.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Dashboard.tsx&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;lazy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Suspense&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Heavy charting lib is NOT in the initial bundle.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// It downloads only when &amp;lt;Chart /&amp;gt; first renders.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Chart&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;lazy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;./HeavyChart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Dashboard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;showChart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setShowChart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;section&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setShowChart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Show analytics&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

      &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;showChart&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Suspense&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;fallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Loading chart…&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Chart&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Suspense&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;section&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💡 &lt;strong&gt;Tip:&lt;/strong&gt; Code-splitting is not just for big libraries. Route-level splitting, loading each page's code only when the user navigates to it, is often the single biggest INP and LCP win, and most frameworks (Next.js, React Router) do it for you automatically once you stop importing everything into one shared bundle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Common mistakes that cost hours
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Optimizing the wrong thing.&lt;/strong&gt; Spending a day shaving 50 ms off an already-green LCP while INP sits in the red. Always fix the worst metric first, measure before you touch anything.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Shipping huge JavaScript bundles.&lt;/strong&gt; Importing an entire library to use one function, or bundling every route's code into one file. This is the number-one cause of bad INP on real devices, your laptop hides it, the phone does not.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Unsized images and embeds causing CLS.&lt;/strong&gt; An &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;img&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; or ad iframe with no width/height reserves zero space, so content reflows and jumps when it loads. Cheap to fix, and a top source of "why does the page keep moving" complaints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Lab-only testing.&lt;/strong&gt; Trusting a single Lighthouse run on your fast laptop and declaring victory. Lab data is for debugging; &lt;strong&gt;field data&lt;/strong&gt; (real users, 75th percentile) is the score that ships. Always check both.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Ignoring fonts.&lt;/strong&gt; A web font that swaps in late pushes text around (CLS) or hides it entirely (delayed LCP). Preload critical fonts and use &lt;code&gt;font-display: swap&lt;/code&gt; with a matched fallback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Takeaways
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The whole article in seven lines&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance is what users &lt;em&gt;feel&lt;/em&gt;, on &lt;em&gt;their&lt;/em&gt; devices, not what your laptop reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Three vitals: &lt;strong&gt;LCP&lt;/strong&gt; (loading, ≤ 2.5 s), &lt;strong&gt;INP&lt;/strong&gt; (interactivity, ≤ 200 ms), &lt;strong&gt;CLS&lt;/strong&gt; (stability, ≤ 0.1).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Always measure with &lt;strong&gt;field data&lt;/strong&gt; at the 75th percentile, not just a lab run.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Loop: measure → find the worst metric → fix one thing → re-measure → repeat.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lazy-load offscreen images (but eager-load the LCP hero) and always set width/height.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Code-split heavy components with dynamic imports so the main thread parses less JS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Most CLS bugs are unsized images, embeds, and late fonts, reserve the space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Where to go next
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Core Web Vitals make the most sense once you understand &lt;em&gt;why&lt;/em&gt; the browser behaves the way it does. If you have not yet, read &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/blog/how-the-browser-renders-a-page" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;How the Browser Renders a Page&lt;/a&gt;, the render path is exactly what LCP and CLS are measuring. Then &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/blog/frontend-build-tooling-and-bundling" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Frontend Build Tooling &amp;amp; Bundling&lt;/a&gt; shows you the mechanics behind code-splitting and shrinking the bundles that wreck INP.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow the full &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/career-paths/frontend-engineer" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Frontend Engineer career path&lt;/a&gt; to put performance in context with the rest of the role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Re-read &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/blog/how-the-browser-renders-a-page" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;How the Browser Renders a Page&lt;/a&gt;, render-blocking resources and layout are the root of LCP and CLS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/blog/frontend-build-tooling-and-bundling" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Frontend Build Tooling &amp;amp; Bundling&lt;/a&gt; to set up route-level code-splitting in your own project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run your own site through PageSpeed Insights today and write down which of the three vitals is your worst, that is your first fix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/blog/core-web-vitals-and-frontend-performance" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;TheSimplifiedTech&lt;/a&gt;, where this guide is interactive, with in-browser terminal labs and diagrams. Learn cloud and DevOps by doing, no videos.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


  React in a Nutshell
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I’m excited to share my book &lt;strong&gt;React in a Nutshell&lt;/strong&gt;, a practical guide designed for developers who want a concise and structured reference for React.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The book covers the essential concepts needed to understand and work effectively with React, including:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Components and props&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;State management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Routing and navigation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Common React mistakes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React Hooks &amp;amp; APIs cheat sheet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The objective of the book is to provide a compact reference that developers can quickly consult while learning React or building applications.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Who is this book for?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This book is suitable for:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Beginners learning React&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frontend developers who want a quick reference&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developers preparing for interviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developers who want to review React concepts efficiently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Get the book
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can find &lt;strong&gt;React in a Nutshell&lt;/strong&gt; here:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://rondatech.gumroad.com/l/react-in-a-nutshell" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://rondatech.gumroad.com/l/react-in-a-nutshell&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Published by &lt;strong&gt;RONDA TECH&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is the product list of a store's admin panel, with a button to delete each product, written the way component library docs and almost every tutorial teach it:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/modules/product/components/ProductList/ProductList.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ProductList&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;refetch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useProducts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isDeleteOpen&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setIsDeleteOpen&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;selected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setSelected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Product&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleDelete&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setSelected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setIsDeleteOpen&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;ul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;li&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleDelete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Delete&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;li&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;ul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DeleteProductDialog&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="na"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isDeleteOpen&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="na"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;selected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="na"&gt;onOpenChange&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;setIsDeleteOpen&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="na"&gt;onDeleted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;refetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The component is correct: it does what it promises, it reads in one pass, and a screen with a single confirmation modal can live like this for years without a single incident. What's worth measuring isn't its behavior, but &lt;strong&gt;where the answer to one specific question lives: which modal is open right now?&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Five points, and they're worth sorting. &lt;strong&gt;The boolean lives in whoever owns the button&lt;/strong&gt;, so the modal's visibility is an implementation detail of the list. &lt;strong&gt;The modal's data is a second piece of state&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;code&gt;selected&lt;/code&gt;, updated on another line, and its type allows it to be &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; while the modal is open. &lt;strong&gt;The modal is mounted next to the button&lt;/strong&gt;, inside the list, even though it isn't part of it. &lt;strong&gt;The &lt;code&gt;refetch&lt;/code&gt; and the close travel through props&lt;/strong&gt; from whoever opens to whoever confirms. Those four are local nuisances: annoying, but reversible with an afternoon's refactor.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fifth is of a different kind: &lt;strong&gt;no place in the app knows which modal is open&lt;/strong&gt;. Every component with a button keeps its own piece of the answer, and the screen can only show one thing at a time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;None of this has an observable cost while there's one screen, one or two modals, and nothing that opens them from outside that screen. It becomes measurable with the third modal, the second place that opens the same one, or the first modal that opens another.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Where this is going
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The destination, raw and not justified yet. Opening a modal is putting a value in the only slot there is:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/modules/product/components/ProductList/ProductList.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleOpenModal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;DeleteProductModalProps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;refetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  Delete
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;A single component, mounted once in the app, decides which modal to render based on the value's class:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/app/Modals.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Modals&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useModal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;instanceof&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;DeleteProductModalProps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DeleteProduct&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;refetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;refetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;instanceof&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;EditProductModalProps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;EditProduct&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="na"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="na"&gt;refetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;refetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="na"&gt;draft&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;draft&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;instanceof&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;CreateCategoryModalProps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CreateCategory&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;prev&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;prev&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onCreate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;onCreate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;And the state of every modal in the app is this:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/modules/modal/context/ModalProvider.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setOpen&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ModalProps&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The parts worth looking at are the &lt;code&gt;draft&lt;/code&gt; of &lt;em&gt;Edit product&lt;/em&gt; and the &lt;code&gt;prev&lt;/code&gt; of &lt;em&gt;New category&lt;/em&gt;: they let a modal open another one and come back without losing what was typed, which is the hard part.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Two costs
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  1. Impossible states are representable
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With a delete modal and an edit modal, the list has two booleans and two &lt;code&gt;selected&lt;/code&gt;. Two booleans are four combinations, and the screen can only show three: none, the delete one, or the edit one. With N modals there are 2^N combinations for N+1 possible screens, plus every one in which the modal is open and its &lt;code&gt;selected&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;None of that fails today, because each &lt;code&gt;handle*&lt;/code&gt; sets both variables in order. What fails is the code written to defend against it: every new modal brings its own &lt;code&gt;if (!product) return null&lt;/code&gt;, a guard against a state the type should never have allowed. The React docs name it as a principle, &lt;em&gt;"Avoid contradictions in state"&lt;/em&gt;, and solve it with a form example that replaces &lt;code&gt;isSending&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;isSent&lt;/code&gt; with a single &lt;code&gt;status&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  2. The modal lives where the button is
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The day &lt;em&gt;Edit product&lt;/em&gt; also has to open from the "Product created" toast, the state moves up to the common ancestor of the list and the toast. With a third place (a keyboard shortcut, the search bar) it moves up again. The second-order effect is that every modal opened from several places ends up with its own context or store, and an app with fifteen modals has fifteen implementations of the same thing: a slot that holds what's open and with what data.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F2u6o7exnj6lmokuhh7oj.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F2u6o7exnj6lmokuhh7oj.png" alt="a component tree. At the top, App; below it, Layout with three branches: ProductList, Toast and Search. ProductList holds two small boxes, " width="800" height="457"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Three components keep their piece of the answer, and two of them mount the same modal.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What's already solved, and what to rule out
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Controlled primitives&lt;/strong&gt; (Radix, Headless UI, the browser's &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;dialog&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;) solve the hard DOM part: focus, inert background, Escape, screen readers. Where their &lt;code&gt;open&lt;/code&gt; lives is left to whoever uses them, and Headless UI says it plainly: &lt;em&gt;"Dialogs are controlled components, meaning that you have to provide and manage the open state yourself"&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The explicit case for keeping it local has an author. Kent C. Dodds classifies &lt;em&gt;"modal isOpen state"&lt;/em&gt; as UI state and, about moving it into a global store, writes: &lt;em&gt;"this is fine for state that is truly global, but for simple state (like whether a modal is open or form input value state) this is a big problem."&lt;/em&gt; He deserves the point in full for a modal that only one button opens: lifting it is paying for indirection and getting nothing back. The argument stops holding with the second place that opens the same modal, which is when &lt;em&gt;what's open&lt;/em&gt; stops being a component's state and becomes the screen's state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;modalType&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;modalProps&lt;/code&gt; in a store&lt;/strong&gt; has been the canonical answer since 2016, when Dan Abramov posted it on Stack Overflow: an action describes which modal you want to see, the reducer stores &lt;code&gt;{ modalType, modalProps }&lt;/code&gt;, and a &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;ModalRoot&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; looks the component up in a map. It's a single slot and it solves both costs. What it brings is a string key and an untyped &lt;code&gt;modalProps&lt;/code&gt;: the compiler doesn't connect &lt;code&gt;'DELETE_POST'&lt;/code&gt; with what that modal needs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Per-component global managers&lt;/strong&gt;, like &lt;code&gt;@ebay/nice-modal-react&lt;/code&gt;, add a promise API (&lt;code&gt;await NiceModal.show(...)&lt;/code&gt;). Their store is an object keyed by id with several modals visible at once, prop typing is partial, and it hasn't published a release since October 2023.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The modal in the URL&lt;/strong&gt; (Next.js &lt;em&gt;intercepting routes&lt;/em&gt;, React Router's &lt;code&gt;backgroundLocation&lt;/code&gt;) makes what's open shareable and resilient to refresh and the back button, at the cost of one route per modal and of everything it needs fitting in the URL.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Family&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Cost 1: impossible states&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Cost 2: the modal lives where the button is&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;A modal that opens another&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Controlled primitives&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;not addressed&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;not addressed&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;the parent stays mounted&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;modalType&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;modalProps&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;solved&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;solved&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;replaces the parent: lost&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;nice-modal-react&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;partial: several visible at once&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;solved&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;the parent stays mounted&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Modal in the URL&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;solved&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;solved&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;one nested route per level&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; the table measures these two costs and nesting, not accessibility, where the primitives win by a wide margin. Verified in October 2026 against React 19.3.0, &lt;code&gt;@ebay/nice-modal-react&lt;/code&gt; 1.2.13, Headless UI 2.2.10, Next.js 16.4.0 and React Router 8.4.0.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Under Abramov's answer is the conversation this article continues. A comment asks to turn the state into a list so you can &lt;em&gt;"open a modal from a modal"&lt;/em&gt; and go back. Abramov replies that he has worked with designers who wanted exclusive modals, &lt;em&gt;"so the approach I wrote up solves accidental nesting"&lt;/em&gt;. And a year later another reader brings up the case neither position solves: a user who has edited some fields, needs a second modal and &lt;em&gt;"will loose the changes he maid"&lt;/em&gt; [sic]. Nobody answers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The thesis
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The React docs have an example that makes this argument without naming modals. An accordion with two panels replaces two &lt;code&gt;isActive&lt;/code&gt; booleans with an index in the parent, and justifies it like this: &lt;em&gt;"Using the active index instead of two “is shown” flags ensured that only one panel is active at a given time."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An open modal is that index at app scale:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Which modal is open is a single piece of data. It's modeled as one slot holding a value (an instance that describes the modal and carries everything it needs to render), not as a boolean per component nor as a stack.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That decides four things when writing code: a class per modal, a single &lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt; in a provider, a single component that mounts the modals, and a shell that doesn't know whether it's open because it only exists while it is.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fd4rmtjqv8j10xl4i4wke.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fd4rmtjqv8j10xl4i4wke.png" alt="the same component tree. App now holds a single box, " width="799" height="411"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The three places write to the same slot, and only one component mounts modals.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The implementation, piece by piece
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  The base class
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The whole file:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/modules/modal/domain/modal-props.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/**
 * Every modal of the app is a subclass. A class and not an interface on purpose:
 * `Modals` narrows with `instanceof`, and interfaces are erased at compile time.
 */&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;abstract&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ModalProps&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;It's empty, and it's the piece that makes the rest work. It gives the slot a common type and, being a class, it exists at runtime: &lt;code&gt;open instanceof EditProductModalProps&lt;/code&gt; narrows the type of &lt;code&gt;open&lt;/code&gt; with no &lt;code&gt;switch&lt;/code&gt;, no &lt;code&gt;as&lt;/code&gt;, and no separate discriminated union with a &lt;code&gt;type: string&lt;/code&gt; field that has to be kept in sync with the components.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  A class per modal
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Everything the modal needs comes in through the constructor, and whoever opens it passes &lt;em&gt;its own&lt;/em&gt; &lt;code&gt;refetch&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/modules/product/domain/modal/product-modal.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;DeleteProductModalProps&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;extends&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ModalProps&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;constructor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;readonly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;readonly&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;refetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;super&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;With this, the impossible state from the opening disappears by construction: there's no way to open the delete modal without a product, because there's no way to build a &lt;code&gt;DeleteProductModalProps&lt;/code&gt; without one.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  The provider and the hook
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The provider is a &lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/modules/modal/context/ModalProvider.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ModalProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ReactNode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setOpen&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ModalProps&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// the slot holds class instances, never functions: `setOpen` would run a function as an updater&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ModalContextValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;handleOpenModal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setOpen&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ModalContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Provider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ModalContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Provider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The comment isn't decoration. &lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt; stores an instance as is, but if it receives a function it runs it as an &lt;em&gt;updater&lt;/em&gt; and stores whatever it returns. That's why what travels in the slot are objects, and the functions a modal needs (the &lt;code&gt;refetch&lt;/code&gt;) go inside them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The hook adds closing, which is setting &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/modules/modal/hooks/useModal.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useModal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleOpenModal&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ModalContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleCloseModal&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleOpenModal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleOpenModal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleOpenModal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleCloseModal&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Opening a modal while another is open replaces it. There's no need to decide what to do with the previous one, because there's no room for it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  &lt;code&gt;Modals&lt;/code&gt;, mounted once
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Modals&lt;/code&gt;, the one from &lt;em&gt;Where this is going&lt;/em&gt;, is mounted only once, inside the provider and outside any screen; never next to a button or inside a row:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/app/App.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ModalProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Products&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ProductList&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Modals&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ModalProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is where the cost is.&lt;/strong&gt; Each modal is a class and an &lt;code&gt;instanceof&lt;/code&gt; branch written by hand, and the compiler doesn't warn you if a class has no branch: the modal simply doesn't render. In exchange, &lt;code&gt;Modals&lt;/code&gt; is the only place that knows the modal components, and whoever opens one only knows the class. When the branches grow, they can be split into one component per feature that &lt;code&gt;Modals&lt;/code&gt; mounts one after another; it's optional and changes nothing else. In the project this pattern comes from, there are 21 classes and 21 branches split that way across three components.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  The shell: its lifecycle is the opening
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The shell never receives an &lt;code&gt;open&lt;/code&gt;. &lt;code&gt;Modals&lt;/code&gt; mounts it when the slot holds its class and unmounts it when it no longer does, so the form's state is born on open and thrown away on close without a single cleanup &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt;. It's built on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;dialog&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;showModal()&lt;/code&gt;, which provide the top layer, the rest of the page made inert, initial focus and implicit &lt;code&gt;aria-modal&lt;/code&gt;. Reduced version, without styles or closing on a backdrop click:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/modules/modal/components/Modal/Modal.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Modal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;labelledBy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onClose&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ref&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;HTMLDialogElement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;handleCloseModal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleCloseSlot&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useModal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleClose&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;onClose&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;onClose&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;else&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleCloseSlot&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// the browser doesn't give the focus back when React removes the dialog: keep the opener&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;opener&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;activeElement&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;HTMLElement&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ref&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;showModal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;style&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;overflow&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;hidden&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;style&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;overflow&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;opener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isConnected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;opener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;focus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Escape fires `cancel` and the browser would close the &amp;lt;dialog&amp;gt; on its own, leaving the&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// slot full: the close goes through the slot instead&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleCancel&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;SyntheticEvent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;HTMLDialogElement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;preventDefault&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleClose&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;dialog&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;ref&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ref&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;aria-labelledby&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;labelledBy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onCancel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleCancel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;dialog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accessibility costs two pieces the browser doesn't provide&lt;/strong&gt;, and both were measured. The first: if &lt;code&gt;cancel&lt;/code&gt; isn't intercepted, Escape closes the native &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;dialog&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; while the slot is still full; the component stays mounted, invisible, with React's state saying it's open. The second: when the dialog is unmounted, focus falls to &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;body&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, not to the button that opened it, which is what the WAI-ARIA modal dialog pattern asks for. Hence the &lt;code&gt;opener&lt;/code&gt; saved on mount. With a &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;div&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; as the container, which is the usual choice, those two come on top of the focus trap, the inert background and the ARIA attributes, all written by hand.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  The modal and its hook
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The component picks the shell, sets the texts and delegates to its hook, which holds the state and the submit:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/modules/product/components/DeleteProduct/DeleteProduct.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;DeleteProduct&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;refetch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleCloseModal&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useModal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleSubmit&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;deleteProduct&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;refetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleCloseModal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;FormModal&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"Delete product"&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;nextText&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"Delete"&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;onSubmit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleSubmit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;“&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;” will be deleted. This can't be undone.&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;FormModal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;First the list that opened the modal is refreshed, then it closes. While &lt;code&gt;loading&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt;, the shell ignores Escape and the backdrop: an operation halfway through isn't cancelled by an accidental gesture.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Back to the inventory
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The boolean that lived in whoever had the button doesn't exist: opening is building a value. Neither does the second piece of state with the data: the data is inside the value and can't be missing. The modal is no longer mounted next to the button but once, in &lt;code&gt;Modals&lt;/code&gt;. The &lt;code&gt;refetch&lt;/code&gt; still travels, but inside the instance, not through props from component to component. And the question of which modal is open now has an answer in a single place, with a type that doesn't allow two.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The acid test: the modal that opens another modal
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Edit product&lt;/em&gt; has its name changed and unsaved, and the category it needs doesn't exist yet. The user clicks &lt;em&gt;New category&lt;/em&gt;, which is a modal with its own form. When it's created, the user has to get back to &lt;em&gt;Edit product&lt;/em&gt; with the name exactly as they left it and the new category already selected; on cancel, with the name and nothing else. It's the case from the unanswered comment under Abramov's answer, and it's the one that breaks the single slot as it stands so far: opening the child replaces the parent, the parent unmounts and its &lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt; is gone.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The obvious way out is a stack&lt;/strong&gt;: a &lt;code&gt;ModalProps[]&lt;/code&gt; that renders all its entries, with the parent mounted under the child and its draft intact. With &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;dialog&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; it works, because the one below becomes inert. But it leaves live state in an array: everything underneath stays mounted, with its effects and its requests, and the implementation has to decide which one is on top, which one gets Escape and what shows up on close. The single slot keeps one live modal and one rule.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The single-slot solution is for the child to receive where to go back to.&lt;/strong&gt; The parent, before it unmounts, puts what has to survive into a new instance of itself:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/modules/product/components/EditProduct/hooks/useEditProduct.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// the parent is about to be unmounted: whatever must survive goes into a new instance of itself&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleNewCategory&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ProductDraft&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;categoryId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleOpenModal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;CreateCategoryModalProps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;EditProductModalProps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;refetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;category&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Category&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;EditProductModalProps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;refetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="na"&gt;categoryId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;category&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;And the parent, when it mounts, starts from that draft if it brings one:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/modules/product/components/EditProduct/hooks/useEditProduct.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;draft&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setPrice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;draft&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;categoryId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setCategoryId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;draft&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;categoryId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;categoryId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The child doesn't know who opened it. It receives &lt;code&gt;prev&lt;/code&gt;, where &lt;em&gt;Cancel&lt;/em&gt; goes back to, and &lt;code&gt;onCreate&lt;/code&gt;, which builds where &lt;em&gt;Create&lt;/em&gt; goes back to, with the new category already selected. Without the imports:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/modules/product/components/CreateCategory/CreateCategory.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;CreateCategory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;prev&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onCreate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Props&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleOpenModal&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useModal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleSubmit&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;category&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createCategory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleOpenModal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;onCreate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;category&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;FormModal&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"New category"&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;nextText&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"Create"&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;onSubmit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleSubmit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClose&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleOpenModal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;prev&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        Category name
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onChange&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;FormModal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;prev&lt;/code&gt; is a &lt;em&gt;memento&lt;/em&gt;: a snapshot of the parent taken right before letting it go. Going back is putting that snapshot in the slot. That's why the same &lt;code&gt;CreateCategory&lt;/code&gt; works for a future &lt;em&gt;Create product&lt;/em&gt; without touching a line: whoever opens it decides where it goes back to.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The cost is stated right here: only what's put into the instance comes back.&lt;/strong&gt; Focus inside the parent, its scroll position, an uncontrolled input or an in-flight request don't travel in &lt;code&gt;prev&lt;/code&gt;, and the parent comes back without them. In practice it forces the state that matters to be controlled and to fit in an object, which is a healthy constraint for a form and bad news for an editor with an undo history.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F9e47l2sy4aubtqb3y3ar.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F9e47l2sy4aubtqb3y3ar.png" alt="two columns with the same three steps: open Edit product, open New category, go back. On the left, the stack: in step two there are two stacked boxes and the draft " width="799" height="491"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In the stack the draft stays alive underneath; with the slot it travels inside the value that says where to go back to.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What didn't change to solve nesting: the provider, the hook, the shell and &lt;code&gt;Modals&lt;/code&gt;. None of them knows a modal can open another, because for them opening and going back are the same operation with a different value.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Caveats, and who this is for
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;There's no exit animation.&lt;/strong&gt; The shell unmounts in the same render in which the slot becomes &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt;, so nothing is left on screen to animate. Libraries that have one keep the last modal precisely for that reason; the &lt;code&gt;@mantine/modals&lt;/code&gt; source explains it in a comment: &lt;em&gt;"Keeping the last one is necessary for providing a clean exit transition."&lt;/em&gt; With the single slot you have to do the same on purpose: delay the &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; until the transition ends.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A modal only exists while it's open, and so does its state.&lt;/strong&gt; That's what makes it unnecessary to clean anything up on close, and it's also what prevents remembering a draft between openings: if &lt;em&gt;Edit product&lt;/em&gt; must recover what was typed after being closed by mistake, that draft has to live outside the modal.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Who it's not for, first: a screen with a single confirmation modal that only one button opens. There, this is a class, a provider and a &lt;code&gt;Modals&lt;/code&gt; component to replace a &lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt;, and the right answer is Kent C. Dodds's: the local &lt;code&gt;open&lt;/code&gt; of the primitive or of the &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;dialog&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. The balance flips with two or more of these conditions: three or more modals, the same modal opened from more than one place, or modals that open modals.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The rule of thumb fits in one line: &lt;strong&gt;if two modals can't be seen at the same time, don't give them two states.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The code
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The runnable project is at &lt;a href="https://github.com/hgomezrobaina/react-modal-slot-example" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;hgomezrobaina/react-modal-slot-example&lt;/a&gt;: the complete product panel, with the pieces from this article and the shell on top of &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;dialog&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, in React 19 and Vite. It starts with &lt;code&gt;npm install &amp;amp;&amp;amp; npm run dev&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What's worth looking at isn't that it starts, but its suite: &lt;strong&gt;ten tests that run in jsdom in about a second, no browser&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;npm test&lt;/code&gt;). That's where what this article claims is checked: that opening a modal while another is open replaces it and never leaves two dialogs, that Escape closes through the slot and not just the native &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;dialog&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, that focus goes back to the button that opened the modal, that the parent unmounts while the child is open, and that &lt;em&gt;New category&lt;/em&gt; returns to &lt;em&gt;Edit product&lt;/em&gt; with the unsaved name and the new category already selected, or with just the name if cancelled. What jsdom doesn't implement (the top layer and the inert background) was checked separately in Chromium.&lt;/p&gt;

